T05.a — Preview 1 host-automation refusal candidate, local Linux, 2026-11-10
Source audit: direct desktop-control, capture and system-control paths ran host
subprocesses without a sandbox handoff; non-hardened legacy shell also allowed
host execution when Trust was absent. These were inconsistent with D5.
Candidate: block direct desktop automation on Windows/macOS regardless of
sandbox availability and block non-hardened legacy shell fallback there. The
canonical isolated shell path remains governed by Trust. Linux unchanged.
Commands on Linux, not native OS confinement evidence:
  bun test test/security test/control test/trust/canonical-shell-isolation.test.ts
    496 pass, 1 skip, 0 fail (before the added service override regression).
  bun test test/security/desktop-control-policy.test.ts test/release/windows-preview-workflow.test.ts
    7 pass, 1 skip, 0 fail (native shell case skipped on Linux).
The Windows/macOS control branches were simulated via process.platform, and a
runner-spy confirmed the control service cannot reach an injected executor.
No Windows or macOS test of this candidate has yet completed; no real desktop
interaction or sandbox escape result is asserted. The policy is scoped to these
paths; it is not proof all OS subprocesses or plugins are sandboxed.
Final combined rerun after adding service-spy and workflow tests:
  bun test test/security test/control test/trust/canonical-shell-isolation.test.ts test/release/windows-preview-workflow.test.ts
    500 pass, 1 native-only skip, 0 fail; root tsc --noEmit exit 0.
